course: dictionary
lesson: 7640
title: One word, many meanings: profile
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one fits. «A kids profile, usually marked with its own picture, shows only films for younger ages.» Here a profile is an online page with a name and picture, not a face seen from the side.
explain: Profile can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it can mean the side view of a face, a short description of a person or place, or the page with your details on a website, app or game. As a verb, to profile someone means to write or collect a description of them.
explain: Some phrases use profile in a special way. «Keep a low profile» means try not to be noticed, and a «high profile» means being well known. Learn these phrases as a set, because their meaning is not just the word profile on its own.
fact: Profile means the side view of a face or head, especially its outline.
fact: A profile can also be a short description of a person, place or company, giving the main facts about them.
fact: On a website, app or game, your profile is the page with your name, picture and information.
fact: «Keep a low profile» means try not to be noticed.
fact: A profile picture may not show who someone really is, so keep your profile private online.
exercise: In art class you draw «a portrait in profile», seen from the side. What does profile mean here? | A map of a town | A picture taken from the front | A short story about a person | * The side view of a face
exercise: «A grown-up's or teenager's profile on a streaming app shows films for their age, not yours.» What is a profile in this sentence? | A drawing of a river from the side | * An account page on an app, with the owner's details | A guess about who did a crime | A list of films in a shop
exercise: Jan says, «She wants to keep a low profile this term.» What does this mean? | She wants to draw faces from the side | * She wants to avoid being noticed | She wants to be famous across the school | She wants to change her profile picture
test: «Our geography book has a profile of the river, showing how its land rises and falls.» What does profile mean here? | * A side-on drawing that shows the shape of the land | A list of animals that live by the water | A photo of the river taken from a plane | A short story about a river
test: Which sentence uses profile to mean a short description? | The app asked for a profile picture | The artist drew her profile in pencil | * The brochure gives a profile of the town, with its main facts | He kept a low profile at the party
exam: Which meaning of profile fits «a high-profile footballer»? | Short and unfriendly | A drawing of the footballer from the side | Hidden from view and quiet | * Well known to many people
